e a bigger part of the  picture now right the drugs are a bigger  part of the picture oh yeah most of not  on death row but regular population most  of the inmates in the regular population  it it maybe didn't come to prison  because of  but drugs was always involved how do you  look at this part of your life that you  that you have I mean there's this  chapter of your life it's certainly very  unusual how do you view it well I guess  I look at it like anybody else looks at  something that they do a farmer or  whatever it's something that I did and I  knew what it was when I took the job  it wasn't no surprise you know I knew  that eventually that I'd have to do that  and now you know I look back on it and I  know I did everything I could to say  that they were treated not just their  death row but all of them they were  treated right wasn't abused and at the  same time no we didn't we didn't let  them to us that way either  but we didn't have that much trouble and  I look back on that is that I did all I  could to be sure they they were treated  right I've met him on the street and  they would run to me with a handout and  you know if somebody might recognize  some of my dating and they'd have to  tell me everything were I've had some of  them tell me you know I die I kept them  from getting in bad trouble in prison  and I knew by something I could gauge  what I did maybe maybe I did all I could  do what was right I don't I don't have  any regrets or anything  and the main thing I mentioned a while  ago I did not let people put me on the  guilt trip  about what I had to do and I did not  allow the inmates problem to become my  problem they had to do what they had to  do I did what I had to do and they just  have to let the rough in Drey all right  charlie  thank you so much for for talking with  me very interesting thank you  you
 

